From: Techniix <Techniix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:38:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] app_server: ReadBitmap(): read front-buffer areas with
 the cursor

The previous change read the software cursor's rectangle from the back
buffer even inside the areas whose current content is only in the front
buffer, using HWInterface::SoftwareCursorFrame(). That is wrong in both
directions:

 * There, the back buffer is stale (direct windows, BWindowScreen) or
   half redrawn (windows in an update session), so the capture would
   get a stale or erased patch the size of the cursor, or of cursor plus
   drag bitmap.
 * SoftwareCursorFrame() returned the fCursorAreaBackup rectangle, which
   _AdoptDragBitmap() only allocates when *not* double buffered, so it
   was always invalid on the path that used it, and the exclusion never
   happened anyway.

Read those areas from the front buffer, software cursor included, as
ReadBitmap() always did, and remove SoftwareCursorFrame(). Outside them
the back buffer is read, which never contains the software cursor.

Remaining limitation: where a software cursor is over a direct window or
a window in an update session, a capture with drawCursor = false
contains it, and one with drawCursor = true contains it twice, as before
the previous change.

Could be squashed into the previous change.

This change was written by an AI assistant (Claude, Anthropic) at the
request of a Haiku user and has only been syntax-checked and reviewed,
not built or run. Haiku's policy does not accept AI-generated
contributions; it is offered as a description of the problem and one
possible fix, for a developer to rewrite or discard.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AVRp8kiTtm6UwGrx2GPsdP
